---
/**
 * @file ui/Seam.astro
 * @description The "=" separator between section panels — delta.dev's
 *              exact markup (plan10.md point 4):
 *
 *   <div class="relative h-4 flex-none overflow-clip border-y">
 *     <div class="px-(--site-section-inset) size-full">
 *       <div class="border-x relative z-1 size-full"></div>
 *     </div>
 *     <svg …45° hatch, full-bleed, stroke-brand-100/80, dark:opacity-5>
 *   </div>
 *
 * WHY THIS SHAPE (what the recording shows):
 * 1. h-4 (16px) with border-y: two hairlines top and bottom SEPARATE the
 *    flush panels — the only horizontal lines in the column.
 * 2. The inner inset border-x box continues the panels' side-lines through
 *    the seam, so the column reads as one instrument channel with a hatched
 *    "danger stripe" across it rather than separate boxes.
 * 3. Hatch (text-hatch = brand-100) spans the FULL band width including the
 *    side insets — matches delta (their seam svg has no inset).
 * 4. flex-none on the stack child: the section stack is a flex column, and
 *    the seam must never stretch (delta verbatim).
 *
 * Where: index.astro renders <Seam /> once after every section except the
 * last (delta's own pattern: seams BETWEEN panels, none at the top/bottom
 * edge — the fixed frame's border-b/t do the edge lines).
 */
---

<div aria-hidden="true" class="relative h-4 flex-none overflow-clip border-y border-line">
  <div class="h-full px-(--site-section-inset)">
    <div class="relative z-1 size-full border-x border-line"></div>
  </div>
  <svg aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 size-full select-none text-hatch dark:opacity-5">
    <defs>
      <pattern id="seam-hatch" width="4" height="4" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" patternTransform="rotate(45)">
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
      </pattern>
    </defs>
    <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#seam-hatch)"></rect>
  </svg>
</div>
